ouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-62-14"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1061016","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a950fa9deb603f45a1080f813766197e767f892058bb6fb9ea34a35d0f978b32","compact":"b7b637078eca0bc2b893e0738ecd4f94820ab74c61273a6b2e827c17a5115e25","nasal":"b7b637078eca0bc2b893e0738ecd4f94820ab74c61273a6b2e827c17a5115e25"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-61-17","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":61,"verse":17,"english":"Having cursed his sons, that best of ascetics then, by all means cheering up the distressed Śunaḥsepa as to his protection, addressed him.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-62-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1061017","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"8ff57c09f23480f69716e6d0d02426e689fabcda57f21f49383e789f2217527a","compact":"de3f9f0de1f292696945e99a6619699899030a2e28427de364d612318e8c8145","nasal":"de3f9f0de1f292696945e99a6619699899030a2e28427de364d612318e8c8145"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-61-18","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":61,"verse":18,"english":"Do you donning on a sacred zone, and wearing a garland of red flowers, and bedaubing your person with red sand paste, hymn Agni with mantras, approaching the Vaisnava sacrificial stake; and, O ascetic's son, (at the same time) chant these two verses in that sacrifice of Amvarisha. Then you will attain success.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.82,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-62-16"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1061018","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f96d953b6ea45e237cb76066eddc083d20d9711a82d6b678cc5c739049f01dfd","compact":"f8ea162b76493bcecaa75f95eabc8591a24a9a18165985100ff8cd3dbedd1e5e","nasal":"f8ea162b7649